<PageShell title="Conclusion">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      As I reflect on my teaching during these first three years, I see course design, assessment, and
      revision as part of an ongoing and intentional cycle of improvement. My courses are structured to
      promote clarity, accessibility, and student engagement, while application-based assignments and
      comprehensive rubrics help students understand expectations and demonstrate their learning in
      meaningful ways. Student feedback, assignment performance, and my own observations have also helped
      me identify areas for growth, including the need for more individualized feedback, expanded
      instructional support for difficult concepts, and stronger assignments that promote authentic
      application rather than superficial completion. Looking ahead, I plan to continue refining these
      courses by replacing less effective activities with more rigorous, student-centered work, developing
      rubrics that support both content mastery and authentic student learning, and taking a more balanced
      approach to artificial intelligence. Rather than focusing only on limiting AI use, I want to help
      students engage with it responsibly and critically by evaluating AI-generated information against
      credible sources and using tools such as BoodleBox within clear instructional guardrails. Together,
      these efforts reflect my commitment to thoughtful course design, academic integrity, and continuous
      growth as an online educator.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageShell>
